WEBVTT

1
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.166
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>explained to Arjuna</b>

2
00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:55.291
<b>how a person following the path </b>
<b>of selfless action (Nishkam Karma Yoga)</b>

3
00:00:55.291 --> 00:01:02.208
<b>develops three qualities: a pure soul, a self-</b>
<b>controlled mind, and mastery over the senses.</b>

4
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:04.708
<b>In these two verses, Lord Krishna</b>

5
00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:11.916
<b>further elaborates on the mental </b>
<b>state and intellect of such a yogi.</b>

6
00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:18.291
<b>In these verses,</b>

7
00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:26.083
<b>Lord Krishna is describing the characteristics </b>
<b>of a yogi who practices Nishkam Karma Yoga.</b>

8
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.708
<b>The first characteristic is that such </b>
<b>a yogi is a knower of the truth,</b>

9
00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:35.375
<b>meaning he understands "who am I".</b>

10
00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:40.541
<b>He is aware of the difference between </b>
<b>his physical body and the soul.</b>

11
00:01:40.541 --> 00:01:45.583
<b>For this reason, he does not consider</b>
<b>himself to be the sole doer.</b>

12
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:52.041
<b>The main characteristic of a Karma Yogi is that </b>
<b>he remains unattached to the fruits of his actions.</b>

13
00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:55.291
<b>Therefore, a Karma Yogi knows</b>

14
00:01:55.291 --> 00:01:58.708
<b>that activities like eating, sleeping, and speaking</b>

15
00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:02.541
<b>are dependent on his physical body and mind.</b>

16
00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:03.875
<b>But the soul,</b>

17
00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:08.875
<b>which is his true self, is </b>
<b>beyond all these activities.</b>

18
00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.208
<b>For example,</b>

19
00:02:10.208 --> 00:02:13.916
<b>a yogi does not eat for taste;</b>

20
00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:17.708
<b>his goal is only to nourish his body.</b>

21
00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:25.416
<b>The body is nourished so that through it, </b>
<b>he can fulfill his duties.</b>

22
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:30.708
<b>A yogi sees his prescribed </b>
<b>duties as his obligation.</b>

23
00:02:30.708 --> 00:02:35.083
<b>When a yogi realizes that he is not the doer,</b>

24
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:39.291
<b>he finds himself free from the </b>
<b>bondage of the results of his actions.</b>

25
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.958
<b>When he is not the real doer,</b>

26
00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:46.083
<b>the consequences of his actions </b>
<b>have no effect on him.</b>

27
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:50.375
<b>This is the state of mind of a Karma Yogi</b>

28
00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:54.500
<b>who has mastered the art of selfless action.</b>

29
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:04.875
<b>Life is synonymous with ups and downs.</b>

30
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:12.208
<b>The highs keep you content, but</b>

31
00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:14.541
<b>as soon as the lows come,</b>

32
00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:25.625
<b>they bring pain like disappointment, </b>
<b>despair, and lack of self-confidence.</b>

33
00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:28.958
<b>If you take a step back</b>

34
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:34.833
<b>and observe your actions and </b>
<b>activities as an impartial spectator,</b>

35
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:41.083
<b>you will understand how you are </b>
<b>bound in these ups and downs.</b>

36
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:46.625
<b>Is it possible to be free from </b>
<b>such emotional fluctuations?</b>

37
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.375
<b>Why not!</b>

38
00:03:48.375 --> 00:03:50.500
<b>It is possible</b>

39
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:56.208
<b>when you observe your life with </b>
<b>an unbiased perspective.</b>

40
00:03:56.208 --> 00:04:03.500
<b>how can you become an impartial </b>
<b>observer of your own actions?</b>

41
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.541
<b>Come</b>

42
00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:07.291
<b>let’s understand this with an example.</b>

43
00:04:07.291 --> 00:04:09.791
<b>When watching a movie,</b>

44
00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:14.916
<b>you get influenced by the character’s events;</b>

45
00:04:14.916 --> 00:04:21.166
<b>your blood pressure and state of </b>
<b>mind become like those characters,</b>

46
00:04:21.166 --> 00:04:22.541
<b>but</b>

47
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:28.916
<b>then you also understand </b>
<b>that this is just a movie.</b>

48
00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:30.583
<b>Why? </b>

49
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:35.208
<b>Because you are an impartial spectator.</b>

50
00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:44.208
<b>You play many different roles as a </b>
<b>mother or father, businessman, or friend.</b>

51
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:54.166
<b>You get entangled in emotional ups and downs </b>
<b>because you are attached to your role.</b>

52
00:04:54.166 --> 00:04:55.541
<b>However,</b>

53
00:04:55.541 --> 00:05:01.916
<b>if you evaluate each of your</b>
<b>roles as an impartial observer,</b>

54
00:05:01.916 --> 00:05:06.416
<b>you can avoid all kinds of emotional bondage.</b>

55
00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:13.208
<b>If you ever have to face </b>
<b>criticism for some reason,</b>

56
00:05:13.208 --> 00:05:20.416
<b>feelings of disappointment, </b>
<b>despair, or humiliation affect you –</b>

57
00:05:20.416 --> 00:05:23.166
<b>take a step back.</b>

58
00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:24.791
<b>Understand</b>

59
00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:33.291
<b>that only your body and mind are </b>
<b>feeling humiliated by that criticism,</b>

60
00:05:33.291 --> 00:05:38.291
<b>not you, that is, the soul.</b>

61
00:05:38.291 --> 00:05:39.541
<b>Because</b>

62
00:05:39.541 --> 00:05:44.250
<b>your true form is the soul,</b>

63
00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.458
<b>not the body or mind.</b>

64
00:05:47.458 --> 00:05:53.000
<b>As soon as you take a step back and </b>
<b>become an impartial observer,</b>

65
00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:00.291
<b>you will surely find freedom from the </b>
<b>emotional turmoil of life's ups and downs.</b>

66
00:06:00.291 --> 00:06:05.625
<b>Such thinking will provide you with </b>
<b>awakened consciousness and restraint,</b>

67
00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:12.375
<b>and you will be able to evaluate</b>
<b>your situation objectively.</b>

68
00:06:17.291 --> 00:06:21.625
<b>Living in a family, it is natural</b>

69
00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:26.125
<b>for us to get entangled in our emotions.</b>

70
00:06:26.125 --> 00:06:30.125
<b>Whether it is a dispute </b>
<b>between husband and wife,</b>

71
00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:35.416
<b>a parent's conflict with their child,</b>

72
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:39.875
<b>or a disagreement with siblings,</b>

73
00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:45.500
<b>all these situations emotionally </b>
<b>give birth to pain within us.</b>

74
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:54.041
<b>And this happens when </b>
<b>we start taking everything very personally.</b>

75
00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:56.208
<b>But</b>

76
00:06:56.208 --> 00:07:04.375
<b>if we observe these events </b>
<b>from a spiritual perspective,</b>

77
00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:11.500
<b>we will not only be able to endure </b>
<b>such situations with ease</b>

78
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.916
<b>but</b>

79
00:07:12.916 --> 00:07:21.583
<b>also keep our family together in </b>
<b>harmony and a heartfelt bond.</b>

80
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:31.833
<b>Consider a situation where a family member </b>
<b>says some harsh words to another;</b>

81
00:07:31.833 --> 00:07:38.708
<b>the practical reaction of the </b>
<b>person hearing those harsh words is,</b>

82
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:42.708
<b>"why did they say that to me?"</b>

83
00:07:42.708 --> 00:07:53.500
<b>In this cycle, the person experiences various</b>
<b>negative emotions and thoughts.</b>

84
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:57.000
<b>And this gives rise</b>

85
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.333
<b>to family quarrels.</b>

86
00:08:00.333 --> 00:08:06.125
<b>But in this same situation, if instead </b>
<b>of reacting emotionally,</b>

87
00:08:06.125 --> 00:08:16.708
<b>that person looks at the situation from a </b>
<b>spiritual perspective rather than a practical one,</b>

88
00:08:16.708 --> 00:08:23.083
<b>perhaps they can save themselves </b>
<b>from this emotional turmoil.</b>

89
00:08:23.083 --> 00:08:30.916
<b>I am trying to tell you all through the Gita</b>

90
00:08:30.916 --> 00:08:38.375
<b>that we are not merely our physical body </b>
<b>or our physical mind;</b>

91
00:08:38.375 --> 00:08:41.416
<b>we are all eternal souls.</b>

92
00:08:41.416 --> 00:08:49.166
<b>That eternal soul is beyond</b>
<b>the temporary situations of life.</b>

93
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:52.958
<b>When we grasp this knowledge,</b>

94
00:08:52.958 --> 00:09:03.208
<b>we can easily understand and </b>
<b>face such temporary situations.</b>

95
00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:12.958
<b>Through this spiritual perspective, you can </b>
<b>easily forgive others for their mistakes,</b>

96
00:09:12.958 --> 00:09:18.583
<b>present your thoughts properly </b>
<b>without getting emotional,</b>

97
00:09:18.583 --> 00:09:25.250
<b>and love others without any ego or attachment.</b>

98
00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:31.708
<b>And these are the foundations </b>
<b>of a beautiful, close-knit family.</b>

99
00:09:31.708 --> 00:09:40.708
<b>So start seeing your family environment</b>
<b>as an impartial observer.</b>

100
00:09:40.708 --> 00:09:43.791
<b>And always remember,</b>

101
00:09:43.791 --> 00:09:47.375
<b>you, who are a real soul,</b>

102
00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:53.333
<b>all your family members who are souls,</b>

103
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:59.041
<b>are beyond this physical, emotional turmoil.</b>

104
00:09:59.041 --> 00:10:06.541
<b>This very knowledge can be the basis </b>
<b>of your harmonious, loving family.</b>

105
00:10:11.458 --> 00:10:18.541
<b>In an ever-changing world, is your </b>
<b>business your identity?</b>

106
00:10:18.541 --> 00:10:20.708
<b>If the answer is yes,</b>

107
00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:23.958
<b>then the answer to the </b>
<b>next question should also be yes.</b>

108
00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:30.291
<b>Is your performance in </b>
<b>your business your identity?</b>

109
00:10:30.291 --> 00:10:34.416
<b>Because your identity is tied </b>
<b>to your performance,</b>

110
00:10:34.416 --> 00:10:43.541
<b>have you started to consider life as moving from </b>
<b>one performance-related worry to another?</b>

111
00:10:43.541 --> 00:10:46.041
<b>Let's take two situations:</b>

112
00:10:46.041 --> 00:10:55.458
<b>while executing a project, either the </b>
<b>result was successful, or you faced failure.</b>

113
00:10:55.458 --> 00:11:00.125
<b>In both situations, you are the same.</b>

114
00:11:00.125 --> 00:11:01.166
<b>But</b>

115
00:11:01.166 --> 00:11:08.416
<b>in failure, you are feeling humiliated </b>
<b>due to the criticism of your colleagues.</b>

116
00:11:08.416 --> 00:11:09.500
<b>And there,</b>

117
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:15.583
<b>in the situation of success, ego </b>
<b>has arisen in you due to praise.</b>

118
00:11:15.583 --> 00:11:20.583
<b>Associating yourself with the </b>
<b>results of your actions is inappropriate.</b>

119
00:11:20.583 --> 00:11:22.458
<b>Your truth is</b>

120
00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:24.625
<b> your soul.</b>

121
00:11:24.625 --> 00:11:26.833
<b>The soul is flawless.</b>

122
00:11:26.833 --> 00:11:32.750
<b>The soul is not affected by humiliation or praise.</b>

123
00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:36.125
<b>It is your body and your mind</b>

124
00:11:36.125 --> 00:11:42.666
<b>that are being influenced by the disguises of </b>
<b>'humiliation and praise'.</b>

125
00:11:42.666 --> 00:11:47.541
<b>Do not tie yourself to the results</b>
<b>of your professional actions;</b>

126
00:11:47.541 --> 00:11:50.125
<b>you will find yourself free.</b>

127
00:11:50.125 --> 00:11:56.750
<b>This does not mean that you have nothing </b>
<b>to do with the results of your actions.</b>

128
00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:00.458
<b>I am saying the exact opposite.</b>

129
00:12:00.458 --> 00:12:04.000
<b>Perform your actions as a duty;</b>

130
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.708
<b>you have control over your actions,</b>

131
00:12:06.708 --> 00:12:08.541
<b>not the results.</b>

132
00:12:08.541 --> 00:12:16.500
<b>The results will only provide information on </b>
<b>whether the process was smooth or flawed.</b>

133
00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.458
<b>This perspective is only possible</b>

134
00:12:19.458 --> 00:12:25.166
<b>when you view every professional </b>
<b>situation objectively.</b>

135
00:12:25.166 --> 00:12:31.458
<b>Only by becoming an impartial observer </b>
<b>can you know the real truth.</b>

136
00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:33.791
<b>Remember,</b>

137
00:12:33.791 --> 00:12:38.500
<b>your soul is your truth,</b>

138
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.458
<b>that is your identity,</b>

139
00:12:41.458 --> 00:12:46.791
<b>not your business or </b>
<b>professional success or failure.</b>

